title: Flagship Dataset of Type 2 Diabetes from the AI-READI Project
description: >-
  A multimodal, AI-ready dataset collected from 2,280 individuals with and without type 2
  diabetes mellitus (T2DM) and harmonised across three data collection sites (University of
  Alabama at Birmingham, University of California San Diego, and University of Washington).
  Data were collected between 19 July 2023 and 1 May 2025 as part of the AI-READI (Artificial
  Intelligence Ready and Equitable/Exploratory Atlas for Diabetes Insights) project, one of four
  Data Generation Projects funded by the NIH Common Fund Bridge2AI program. Recruitment sampling
  aimed at an approximately equal distribution of participants across diabetes severity, sex and
  self-reported race/ethnicity, and the acquisition protocol spans multiple domains: survey data,
  physical measurements, clinical laboratory data from blood and urine, 12-lead electrocardiography,
  cognitive screening, monofilament testing of peripheral neuropathy, vision testing, retinal
  imaging (colour fundus photography, fundus autofluorescence, near-infrared reflectance, OCT,
  OCTA and fluorescence lifetime imaging ophthalmoscopy), continuous glucose monitoring, wearable
  physical activity monitoring, and home environmental sensing. This public release contains no
  protected health information; information on sex, race/ethnicity and medications used has been
  removed and is held under controlled access. Version 3.0.0 comprises 356,343 files totalling
  approximately 3.82 TB.
