future_use_impacts:
  - impact_details: >-
      There is a theoretical risk of future re-identification. AI algorithms can infer individual
      patient characteristics and could facilitate individual-level identification. To prevent
      re-identification attempts the project implements a robust data dissemination system, a strict
      licence agreement, and data watermarking for both the public and the controlled sets.
  - impact_details: >-
      Because enrolment is ongoing, interim data releases may not have achieved the intended balanced
      distribution across race/ethnicity, sex and diabetes severity; models developed on this version
      may therefore not exhibit the balance the final cohort is designed to provide.
  - impact_details: >-
      Recruitment was predominantly urban and hospital-based through three academic health systems
      and may not fully capture diverse cultural and socioeconomic backgrounds. The cohort does not
      include other races/ethnicities such as Pacific Islanders and Native Americans, which limits
      the generalisation of derived models.
  - impact_details: >-
      Requiring that participants speak and read English restricts the population represented and may
      have created challenges in recruiting Hispanic and/or Asian persons.

acquisition_methods:
  - acquisition_details: >-
      Directly observed measurements taken during the in-person study visit and from at-home devices:
      vital signs and anthropometrics, clinical laboratory assays of blood and urine, 12-lead ECG,
      monofilament testing, vision testing, retinal imaging, continuous glucose monitoring, wearable
      activity monitoring and home environmental sensing.
    was_directly_observed: true
    was_inferred_derived: false
    was_reported_by_subjects: false
  - acquisition_details: >-
      Participant-reported data collected through self-administered questionnaires in REDCap
      (screening, demographics, CES-D-10, PAID-5, diabetes self-care score, dietary assessment,
      ophthalmic survey, smoking/alcohol/vaping/marijuana use, general health, social determinants of
      health, and current medications). Verification of data entry was performed where possible, for
      example by cross-referencing entered medications with medications physically brought in or
      photographed by the participant.
    was_directly_observed: false
    was_reported_by_subjects: true
    was_validated_verified: true
  - acquisition_details: >-
      Derived and calculated values, including waist-hip ratio and body mass index computed from
      measured height, weight and circumferences, and calculated low-density lipoprotein cholesterol,
      globulin and A/G ratio from measured laboratory values.
    was_inferred_derived: true

collection_mechanisms:
  - mechanism_details: >-
      REDCap electronic data capture, used for the recruitment interface, electronic consent,
      participant-reported questionnaires, and clinical data entered at the visit (medications
      assessment, vitals, visual acuity, contrast sensitivity, monofilament test results and complete
      blood count results). Range and skip-pattern checks were configured in REDCap.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Philips PageWriter TC30 Cardiograph (Amsterdam, The Netherlands), used for the 12-lead
      electrocardiogram with the participant reclining or supine and the position recorded (0, 30, 60
      or 90 degrees relative to supine). Data exported as .xml and converted to the WaveForm DataBase
      (WFDB) standard.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Dexcom G6 continuous glucose monitor (Dexcom, Inc., San Diego, California), applied to the
      abdomen and worn continuously for 10 days after the visit, recording blood glucose in mg/dL
      every 5 minutes. Participants were masked to the results during the monitoring period.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Garmin Vivosmart 5 physical activity monitor (Garmin Ltd, Schaffhausen, Switzerland), worn for
      10 days, capturing steps, heart rate, respiratory rate, sleep duration and phases, oxygen
      saturation, stress level and activity calories. Exported in .FIT format and converted to the
      Open mHealth standard.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Custom-designed home environmental sensor (the LeeLab Anura, Karalis Johnson Retina Center,
      University of Washington), placed in the participant's home for 10 days, recording ambient
      temperature, relative humidity, nitrogen oxides (NO and NO2), volatile organic compounds,
      particulate matter (PM1.0, PM2.5, PM4, PM10) and eleven multi-spectral light intensity
      measurements. The sensor and the fitness tracker were chosen with participant privacy as a
      primary concern: they capture no video or audio, have no GPS location monitoring and are not
      synced with participant-owned devices.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Optomed Aurora IQ handheld fundus camera (Optomed, Oulu, Finland), used for undilated
      macula-centred and disc-centred colour fundus photography (4 images per participant); image
      quality varies because the eye is undilated and the camera is handheld.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      iCare EIDON widefield TrueColor confocal fundus system (iCare USA, Inc., Raleigh, North
      Carolina), used in fully automated mode for ultra-widefield central, nasal and temporal colour
      fundus photography, central infrared and fundus autofluorescence imaging, and a mosaic of
      ultra-widefield images (12 images per participant).
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Heidelberg Spectralis HRA optical coherence tomography and OCT angiography system (Heidelberg
      Engineering GmbH, Heidelberg, Germany), used for optic nerve head radial circle high-resolution
      OCT, posterior pole macula high-resolution 61-line OCT and 20x20 high-speed 512-line macular
      OCTA (6 images per participant).
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Topcon Maestro2 3D OCT-1 (Topcon Healthcare, Itabashi-ku, Tokyo, Japan), used for 3D wide
      12x9 512x128 OCT, 3D macula 6x6 512x128 OCT and 6x6 360x360 macular OCTA; exported in .fda
      format and converted to DICOM for the dataset (6 images per participant).
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Topcon Triton DRI swept-source OCT (Topcon Healthcare, Itabashi-ku, Tokyo, Japan), used for
      3D(H)+radial 12x9 512x256 OCT and 6x6 and 12x12 macular OCTA; exported in .fda format and
      converted to DICOM (6 images per participant).
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Carl Zeiss Meditec Cirrus 5000 (Jena, Germany), used for 200x200 disc cube OCT, 512x128 macula
      cube OCT, and 6x6 macular and disc OCTA (8 images per participant).
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Heidelberg fluorescence lifetime imaging ophthalmoscopy (FLIO) system (Heidelberg Engineering
      GmbH, Heidelberg, Germany), used for macula-centred imaging (2 images per participant);
      exported in .sdt format and converted to DICOM. FLIO was performed last in the visit because it
      takes longer and exposes participants to uncomfortable light levels.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Vision testing instruments: M&S Technologies Electronic Visual Acuity tester (Niles, Illinois)
      for photopic and mesopic best-corrected letter acuity at 4 metres, using a 2.0 neutral density
      filter for the mesopic condition; Mars letter contrast sensitivity chart (Mars Perceptrix,
      Chappaqua, New York) read monocularly under photopic and mesopic conditions; Topcon KR-800
      autorefractor/keratometer (Topcon Healthcare) for autorefraction; and NIDEK LM-600P, Topcon
      CL-200 or Topcon CL-300 lensometers.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Montreal Cognitive Assessment (MoCA) administered electronically on an iPad using the MoCA Duo
      application (MoCA Cognition, Quebec, Canada), producing a total score, section subscores, a
      Memory Index Score and task completion times exported as .csv.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Peripheral neuropathy assessed with a standard 10 g monofilament applied to three locations on
      the plantar surface of each foot, ten times per location, with the participant's eyes closed
      and responding yes/no; insensate areas were retested for confirmation.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Automatic oscillometric, medically approved blood pressure devices used across sites: OMRON
      HEM 907XL, Medline MDS4001 automatic digital blood pressure monitor, and Welch Allyn 6000
      series vital signs monitor with FlexiPort reusable cuff. Systolic and diastolic blood pressure
      and heart rate were measured twice, separated by 2 minutes.
  - mechanism_details: >-
      Clinical laboratory testing. Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments-certified laboratories
      local to each site performed complete blood count testing on fresh whole blood; all other
      assays were performed by the University of Washington Nutrition and Obesity Research Center
      (NORC) testing facility on stored frozen samples, with results provided in .csv format.

