data_collectors:
  - role: Clinical research coordinator
    collector_details: >-
      Coordinators at the three sites recruited, consented and enrolled participants and performed the
      protocol elements. All research personnel underwent training by the data manager at UAB and
      worked from a detailed Manual of Procedures; a certification process was required, including
      mandatory institutional compliance training for human subject research and the successful
      administration of all protocol elements to at least three volunteer practice subjects.
  - role: Data manager
    collector_details: >-
      A data manager at each site oversaw the training and certification process and was responsible
      for quality control of all data before upload to the FAIRhub platform.
  - role: Phlebotomist and laboratory assistant
    collector_details: >-
      Responsible for blood collection from participants and for local processing and shipping of
      plasma, serum, buffy coats, PAXgene RNA tubes and CPT mononuclear cell preparation tubes.
  - role: Clinical laboratory
    collector_details: >-
      Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments-certified laboratories local to each site performed
      complete blood count analysis on fresh whole blood on the day of collection.
  - role: Central laboratory
    collector_details: >-
      The University of Washington Nutrition and Obesity Research Center (NORC) performed HbA1c,
      NT-proBNP, troponin-T, C-peptide, insulin, high-sensitivity CRP, chemistry, lipid and urine
      assays on samples stored at -70 degrees Celsius and batch-shipped on dry ice approximately once
      per quarter.
  - role: Biorepository
    collector_details: >-
      The University of Alabama at Birmingham Center for Clinical and Translational Science operates
      the central study-wide biobank, receiving plasma, serum, buffy coats, PAXgene RNA vacutainers
      and CPT tubes from all three sites and performing genomic DNA extraction and PBMC isolation and
      cryopreservation.
  - role: Central data curation team
    collector_details: >-
      After data were sent from the study sites, the central project team performed additional
      processing for dissemination, including mapping to standardized terminologies and preparation of
      the released dataset on FAIRhub.

direct_collection:
  - is_direct: true
    collection_details: >-
      Data were collected directly from participants at the three recruiting sites during a single
      in-person visit lasting between 2.5 and 4 hours, plus a 10-day at-home monitoring period.
      Recruitment pools were identified indirectly by screening electronic health records at each site
      for diabetes and prediabetes ICD-10 codes among patients who had had an encounter with the
      sites' health systems.

sampling_strategies:
  - is_sample: true
    is_random: false
    is_representative: false
    why_not_representative: >-
      The cohort is intentionally triple-balanced by self-reported race/ethnicity (Asian, Black,
      Hispanic, White), diabetes presence and severity (no diabetes; pre-diabetes or
      lifestyle-controlled; controlled by oral or non-insulin injectable medication; insulin
      controlled) and biological sex, rather than targeting the demographic distribution of the US
      population, because balanced training data are considered critical for developing unbiased
      machine learning models. Recruitment is predominantly urban and hospital-based through three
      academic health systems, participants are volunteers (volunteer bias), participation requires
      the ability to speak and read English, and other groups such as Pacific Islanders and Native
      Americans are not included. The FAIRhub study metadata records the sampling method as
      "Non-Probability Sample".
    representative_verification: >-
      Composition of participants is monitored during recruitment in terms of diversity and inclusion
      and is adjusted by under- and oversampling groups as needed; recruitment proceeds in waves whose
      composition and size are influenced by the observed participation characteristics of
      race/ethnicity, gender, T2DM severity and site. Uniform data collection protocols were
      implemented for all subjects across all study sites to minimise sampling bias.

instances:
  - counts: 2280
    label_description: >-
      No explicit label or target is associated with each data instance. The dataset is hypothesis
      agnostic and was designed to facilitate multiple potential downstream AI/ML applications, so no
      labelling was performed.
    missing_information: >-
      Not all modalities are available for all participants. Some participants elected not to
      participate in some study elements. In a few cases the data collection device had no stored
      results or was returned too late to retrieve results (for example the battery died or data were
      lost), and in a few cases a data collision at some point in the process resulted in lost data.

relationships:
  - relationship_details: >-
      All instances are part of the same prospective data generation project (AI-READI). There is
      currently only one study visit per participant, so instances in this version are not linked
      longitudinally; approximately 10 per cent of the cohort is planned to be invited for a follow-up
      visit in year 4 of the project.

